:1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX019\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that an ICAV umbrella may prepare separate financial statements per sub-fund and that its board may dispense with AGMs. Contrasts this with umbrella-level accounts and generally mandatory AGMs for the investment plc. Matches HO-05-Irish-ICAV and HO-05-Irish-investment-plc.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that an ICAV is not a per se corporation and can check-the-box to be a partnership. States that the investment plc is on the per se corporation list and cannot elect. Matches HO-05-bank Tax treatment and both vehicle excerpts.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required minimums are fully covered with the correct orientation, and neither central error (reversed eligibility) is present. Several side claims go beyond the supplied evidence: unanimous written consent to dispense with a plc AGM, shareholder or auditor rights to requisition an ICAV AGM, and the disregarded-entity option. None is contradicted by the sources, so they are unsupported extras rather than material falsehoods. The PFIC remark is supported by HO-05-bank, and 'most new Irish ETF umbrellas are ICAVs' is consistent with 'usually an Irish ICAV'.\"}","ttft_ms":3987,"type":"result","duration_ms":7939,"uuid":"d20bf3a4-6695-40b5-82c5-e631542828a2","ttft_stream_ms":564,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":564,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
